s in southeastern New York. In addition, the company operates 552 circuit miles of transmission lines; 16 transmission substations; 63 distribution substations; 89,675 in-service line transformers; 3,764 pole miles of overhead distribution lines; and 2,417 miles of underground distribution lines, as well as 4,374 miles of mains and 379, 939 service lines for natural gas distribution. Further, it invests in electric and gas transmission projects. The company primarily sells electricity to industrial, commercial, residential, and government customers. Consolidated Edison, Inc. was founded in 1823 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy P. Cawley | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 60 | Compensation: $4.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Consolidated Edison, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $43.8B market cap on $16.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 5% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.12413789993497697},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","64 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Consolidated Edison (NYSE:ED) Sets New 12-Month High \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/consolidated-edison-nyseed-sets-new-12-month-high-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793998864.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Consolidated Edison Inc $ED Stock Holdi